%% UrbanRide end-to-end ride request sequence
%% Target file: diagrams/seq-01-ride-request.png
%% Annotated with the latency budget from ADD section 5.3
%% Critical path total ~210ms, headroom ~290ms to the 500ms SLA.
%% NOTE: the Graphviz original was not a true sequence diagram - it had no
%% lifelines. This version does, which is why it is worth redrawing.

sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Rider as Rider App
    participant GW as API Gateway
    participant ME as Matching Engine
    participant R as Redis
    participant RS as Routing Service (OSRM)
    participant TMS as Trip Management Service
    participant BS as Billing Service
    participant NS as Notification Service
    actor Driver as Driver App

    Rider->>GW: POST /rides [REST/HTTPS]
    activate GW
    Note over GW: Auth + rate-limit check<br/>~20ms
    GW->>ME: gRPC RideRequest
    deactivate GW
    activate ME

    Note over ME: lat/lng to H3 res-8 cell<br/>K-ring(1) = 7 cells, under 1ms

    ME->>R: SMEMBERS (pipelined, K-ring cells)
    R-->>ME: ~30 candidate driver IDs (~2-5ms)

    ME->>RS: gRPC table(30 origins) [many-to-one ETA]
    RS-->>ME: duration_sec[] ranked (~50-80ms)

    ME->>R: GET surge:h3:{cell}
    R-->>ME: multiplier (~5ms)

    ME->>TMS: gRPC CreateTrip (status=Requested)
    activate TMS
    TMS-->>ME: trip_id (PostgreSQL write ~30ms)

    ME->>R: SET NX driver:{id}:assignment = trip_id
    R-->>ME: OK, atomic CAS won (~20ms)
    deactivate ME

    TMS->>TMS: UpdateTrip (status=Matched)

    Note over Rider,Driver: Critical path ends here: ~210ms of the 500ms SLA

    TMS-)BS: Kafka trip.events (async)
    deactivate TMS
    activate BS
    BS->>BS: Authorise payment hold [Saga pivot]
    BS-)BS: REST/HTTPS to payment gateway
    deactivate BS

    TMS-)NS: Kafka trip.events (async)
    activate NS
    NS->>Driver: WebSocket dispatch offer
    NS->>Rider: WebSocket live driver position + ETA
    deactivate NS
